From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Turnip Thor <thor@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:56:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tu: Banana Native (nxnative) profile hook

An empty profile for applicationName "nxnative" (Banana Native, the
Switch 2 compatibility layer), with its own marker for the test builds,
like the Eden one: sysmem or nolrz for that app only, to find where the
black streaks in Ocarina of Time come from.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KggzvL8zXAkzHKvMM3vhEZ
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf b/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf
index 22a076699fe..91813da9b4c 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf
@@ -215,5 +215,15 @@
         <application name="yuzu-based emulators (Eden)" application_name_match="^yuzu Emulator$">
             <option name="tu_debug" value="" /> <!-- eden-debug -->
         </application>
+        <!--
+            Banana Native / nxnative, the Switch 2 compatibility layer
+            (applicationName "nxnative"). Nothing changes by default; the
+            thor-test-* builds fill the "nxnative-debug" marker the same way,
+            to tell whether the wide black streaks Ocarina of Time shows while
+            the camera moves come from GMEM (sysmem) or LRZ (nolrz).
+        -->
+        <application name="Banana Native (nxnative)" application_name_match="^nxnative$">
+            <option name="tu_debug" value="" /> <!-- nxnative-debug -->
+        </application>
     </device>
 </driconf>
-- 
